A||||1||Shaun41178||Dyno results for ported TB||||14||
Z||000000||Shaun41178||01-27-2000||02:43 PM||||Well I have the dyno results for the ported Tb for the V6.  You guys are welcome.  The ported TB gave about 1-2 more hp and 2-3 more torque throughout the rpm band with a maximum increase 4 hp.  this was on a stock internal 2.8 engine.  This was just the ported tb that was added.  if you port out the top intake to match the TB then you can probably expect to see another 1-2 hp increase.<P>With a modified 2.8 or a 3.2 or even a 3.4 you can expect to see even larger increases.  I would say that with a 3.2 power will jump 5 hp throughout the rpm band.<P>I have the dyno sheet but have yet to scan it into my webpage.<P>Just thought you guys might want to know.  Again your all welcome.||||reg||14
Z||000001||Alex4mula||01-27-2000||03:11 PM||||Good results! Thanks for sharing it. Could you explain the porting procedure? How much (mm or inches)? You did it yourself? Machine shop? Cost$$?||||reg||1
